# DOL-X line-ending policy
# Text files are normalized to LF in the repository and checked out as LF,
# so line endings no longer depend on each machine's core.autocrlf setting.
# Binary types are listed explicitly so they are never line-ending normalized.

# Default: treat as text, store and check out as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text files without a conventional extension.
LICENSE text eol=lf
LICENSE2 text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.bmp binary
*.zip binary
*.rar binary
*.7z binary
*.gz binary
*.jar binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
